    "methods_description": "Simultaneous EEG, electrospinography (ESG), electroneurography (ENG), and electromyography (EMG) recordings were acquired from 26 participants during nine conditions: resting state (eyes open), mixed median nerve stimulation, mixed tibial nerve stimulation, sensory stimulation of individual fingers (index, middle) and toes (first, second), and combined digit stimulation. Recordings included electrocardiographic and respiratory signals. EEG channel Fz was referenced to both right mastoid (standard EEG reference) and the 6th thoracic vertebra (ESG reference).",
